[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0m[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what was changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two issues were found and fixed:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### 1. Build failure: OpenSSL dependency (rng.rs + Cargo.toml)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation used the [38;5;10mopenssl[0m crate for AES-256-ECB encryption in the DRBG (deterministic random bit generator). This required system OpenSSL development libraries which weren't available. Replaced with the pure-Rust [38;5;10maes[0m crate — functionally identical, no system dependencies needed.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### 2. Wrong output: [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m called with bit counts instead of byte counts (hash.rs + main.rs)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This was the core correctness bug. The C [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m function's [38;5;10mdatalen[0m parameter is nominally in [1mbits[22m (it uses [38;5;10mdatalen >> 3[0m to get bytes, [38;5;10mbuflen[0m tracks bits, etc.). However, the callers in [38;5;10mhash_blake.c[0m and [38;5;10mPQCgenKAT_sign.c[0m pass [1mbyte counts[22m directly:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mc
[0m[38;5;10m// C code in hash_blake.c — passes SPX_N (16), a byte count
blakeX_update(&S, sk_prf, SPX_N);

// C code in PQCgenKAT_sign.c — passes sizeof tag - 1 (23), a byte count  
blakeX_update(ctx, tag, sizeof tag - 1);
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The one-shot [38;5;10mblake256()[0m wrapper correctly multiplies by 8 ([38;5;10mblake256_update(&S, in, inlen*8)[0m), but the incremental callers do not. This is an intentional (if confusing) pattern in the C code — the KAT test vectors were generated with this behavior.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation "fixed" this by multiplying by 8 everywhere:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// Old Rust (WRONG — doesn't match C behavior)
blake256_update(&mut s, &sk_prf[..SPX_N], (SPX_N as u64) * 8);
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This caused the BLAKE-256 hash to process different amounts of data than the C code, producing completely different cryptographic outputs. The fix was to pass byte counts, matching the C callers:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// Fixed Rust (matches C behavior)
blake256_update(&mut s, &sk_prf[..SPX_N], SPX_N as u64);
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This change was applied to all [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m calls in [38;5;10mhash.rs[0m (3 call sites in [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m, 3 in [38;5;10mhash_message[0m) and [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m (all KAT transcript functions).[0m[0m
